WEBVTT

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.560
Okay! Next is...

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.730
Master, I've finished the cleaning.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.050
Is there anything else I can do?

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.360
Yeah, Aletta-san, the next 
thing I'd like you to do is...

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.920
That smell... Is it...

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.350
Corn potage!

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.390
Wow, it smells fantastic!

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.740
A friend of mine gave me a bunch of corn.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.510
We're going to serve this 
instead of miso soup today.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.710
Oh, I see!

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:00.880
I'm finished.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.290
Thanks, Kuro. Good work.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.290
<i>I still can't get used to her telepathy.</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.050
Chicken curry.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.530
I'm so glad.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.430
Of course I have some ready.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.190
Okay, it's just about time to open.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.190
Right!

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:28.210
Right.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.560
Welcome!

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:12.960
<b>Empire</b>

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:21.830
Hmm... This is all the 
requests they have today?

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.210
Escorting a merchant to the harbor...

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:27.270
Killing giant rats, killing goblins...

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.660
None of them are worth more than 
a little pocket change, but...

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.450
Hey, Hilda!

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.230
What's that? Goblin-killing?

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.920
You won't have to take piddly jobs like 
that if you join my mercenary team!

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.440
Who would ever want to join your team?

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.330
Say what?! I'm not gonna offer again!

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.720
Good evening. You sure told him.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:58.090
You don't need anyone's help, huh?

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.720
Ranija... Alicia.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.420
Hmph. You two are a lot like me, aren't you?

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:09.530
But really? The great Hilda the 
Night Strider, going after goblins?

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:13.400
Is a reward like this even worth the effort?

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.340
You can't be sure it's such 
a useless job just yet.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.150
There are more of them than I expected.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.620
I managed to find their nest.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.980
I should be able to finish this tomorrow.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.140
I think that's the last of them.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.790
Reporting back to the village 
can wait until after nightfall.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:42.630
I'm going to try to find 
their treasure first.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:48.030
The last horde of goblins I wiped 
out only had a bunch of junk.

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:52.660
I hope these guys have something 
that's worth at least a little money.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.290
<b>Western
Restaurant
Nekoya</b>

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.790
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:02.930
What is this?

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:11.800
I don't know what it is, but...

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.730
Oh! Welcome!

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.870
Corn potage...

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.290
Not eggs...

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.240
What is this place?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.050
Is something wrong?

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.220
Are you a demon?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.510
Huh?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.020
Oh, uh... I...

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.970
No, forget I asked. I'm sorry.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.800
I'm a demon, too.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.350
My name is Hilda.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.940
I work here. My name is Aletta.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.680
Aletta...

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.450
What is this place?

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.530
It looks like a pub or a restaurant...

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.450
This is Western Restaurant Nekoya.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:20.100
It's in a different world 
from the one we live in.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:25.770
The master says it opens once every 
seven days, on the Day of Satur.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:26.210
<b>Western
Restaurant
Nekoya</b>

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:30.720
Our customers call it the 
Restaurant to Another World.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.480
The Day of Satur?

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.030
Another world?

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:39.440
Now that you mention it, there are 
many things here I've never seen.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:43.910
Well, if you're a restaurant, 
you must have food.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.610
Now that I know that, there's no problem.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:50.510
Yes! All of the food here is incredibly good!

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.740
Can you read the Eastern 
Continent's language?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.780
I can.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.720
Then here's our menu.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.300
I'll bring you your complimentary 
water and wet hand towel.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.530
Wow, there's a lot to choose from.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.970
They can make croquettes and fries, too?

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.890
What?! They even have dessert?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.960
And it's so affordable!

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.740
In the capital, this would 
cost a few gold coins,

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:24.000
but here, it's only a few coppers.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.020
And ordering something with a 
drink is an even better deal.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:32.160
But I should probably order something 
that'll fill my belly first...

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.910
Cheesecake?!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.180
A baked dessert made with plenty of cheese?

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.410
I love cheese, but I've 
never had it as a dessert.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:46.100
Thank you for waiting. Here's your
 water and wet hand towel.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.230
Aletta...

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:48.420
Yes?

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.760
A soufflé cheesecake, please.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.680
With this so-called "black tea."

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.670
Of course! Thank you!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.150
Another pork cutlet rice bowl!

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.180
That was quick...

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:07.790
<i>All the customers seem 
to be enjoying the food.</i>

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.820
<i>Maybe I can expect the same luxury?</i>

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.190
More teriyaki chicken, please.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:15.210
And another cup of seishu.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.820
Another draft beer for me, please.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.750
<i>Are they samurai?</i>

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.280
You are quite the drinker, as always.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.170
<i>Isn't that the samurai master, Tatsugoro?!</i>

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:28.400
<i>And next to him... Is that 
the Great Sage Artorius?!</i>

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.930
<i>The legendary mercenary 
that the bards sing about</i>

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.560
<i>and the world's greatest sage...</i>

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:38.990
<i>are eating together in the same place?</i>

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:43.220
<i>Soufflé Cheesecake</i>

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.390
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.220
Here's your soufflé cheesecake.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.730
And this is the black tea that comes with it.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.850
That blue jar contains sugar.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.510
Help yourself if you'd like.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:54.460
Help myself? I can just use 
as much sugar as I want?

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:55.390
Of course.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.240
Please enjoy.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.680
<i>It's sugar, all right.</i>

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.320
<i>It's so white.</i>

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.750
<i>But sugar is usually brown...</i>

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:15.320
<i>It's good!</i>

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.700
<i>There's a hint of bitterness and sourness,</i>

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.420
<i>but the sugar mellows it out.</i>

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.160
<i>It's a flavor I'm not used to,</i>

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:25.050
<i>but it feels like it's soaking 
into every inch of my tired body.</i>

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:28.060
<i>Okay, next is...</i>

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.430
<i>It has the sourness and aroma of cheese,</i>

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:39.900
<i>but it's definitely sweet!</i>

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:42.240
<i>And this texture...</i>

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.540
<i>It's soft, but it falls apart in my mouth.</i>

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:51.400
<i>I know I ate a bite, but only 
the aftertaste is still there!</i>

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.040
<i>I can't get enough of this!</i>

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.360
<i>This purple sauce is exquisite, too.</i>

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.050
<i>Is it berries boiled with sugar?</i>

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.880
<i>And eating the two together 
makes it taste even better!</i>

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:12.860
<i>The bittersweet berry sauce is a 
perfect match with the cheesecake.</i>

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:16.980
<i>This rich sweetness that you 
don't get from raw fruit</i>

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.830
<i>combines with the two different sour 
flavors of the cheese and berries,</i>

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:23.320
<i>creating a perfect harmony!</i>

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:31.610
<i>And it pairs wonderfully with the black tea!</i>

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:36.280
<i>And this is all they charge 
for such perfection?</i>

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.380
<i>It's a far better deal than 
desserts in the capital!</i>

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.080
<i>And above all, it's delicious!</i>

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:41.940
Aletta.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.930
Yes?

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.260
Another soufflé cheesecake!

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.930
No... Make it three more!

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:51.060
And a refill on the tea, too!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.060
Of course!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.310
Please wait just a moment!

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.240
Thank you very much!

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.820
I thought I'd just make some pocket change,

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:18.420
but I stumbled upon quite the amazing place.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.620
Maybe I'll tell them about it one day.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:26.240
It's never a bad thing to be owed a favor.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.850
Thank you very much.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:38.390
Aletta-san, Kuro, it's pretty late.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.480
Sit tight. I'll make you dinner.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:41.560
Okay!

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:42.550
Very well.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.240
Here you go.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:52.730
Ah, it smells so good!

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:55.390
Master, what is this dish called?

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:56.920
It's fried rice.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.630
I worked part-time at a Chinese restaurant 
for two years in high school.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.120
That's when I started devoting myself to—

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.630
Chinese? High school?

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:07.400
Oh, sorry. Never mind.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.030
I'll bring you some soup.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.390
Okay!

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:12.790
<i>Soup!</i>

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.170
<i>Maybe it'll be that lovely yellow,</i>

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:19.120
<i>slightly sweet one with 
the light, milky flavor...</i>

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.030
<i>The corn potage he was 
preparing this morning?</i>

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.340
Here you go. Chinese soup.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:27.530
<i>It wasn't...</i>

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.370
What's wrong?

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.530
Uh, nothing! Nothing at all!

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:36.610
Thank you, god of demons, 
for this, my daily bread.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:38.320
I shall now partake.

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:41.220
As will I.

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:51.810
<i>The aroma of galeo... er, garlic? 
Spreads throughout my mouth,</i>

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.100
<i>and the texture is so unique.</i>

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:57.220
<i>The rice grains are enveloped 
in a thin layer of egg,</i>

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.730
<i>making it sort of... crumbly?</i>

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.860
<i>And all the bits and pieces 
cut into uniform sizes</i>

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:07.450
<i>keep their own unique flavors while 
still blending into the dish.</i>

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.170
This fried rice is really delicious!

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:12.580
Glad to hear it.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:16.010
This kind of seasoning is new to me.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:18.330
So this is "Chinese"?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.250
Would you like to try some, Kuro-san?

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.160
It's fried rice!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.710
<i>It looks similar to the 
rice used in chicken curry.</i>

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:31.600
<i>Aletta says the fried rice is delicious.</i>

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.180
<i>The chicken curry is also delicious.</i>

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.600
<i>Perhaps...</i>

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.370
Master, do fried rice and curry go together?

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.100
I'm not sure...

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:42.750
What do you say?

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:49.730
I'll pass.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:52.130
But it's so good!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.550
This Chinese soup is good, too!

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:59.380
Master, more chicken curry, please.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:00.170
Comin' right up.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:04.120
I'll see you again on the next Day of Satur.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:06.160
Yup. See you then.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.280
Well, I'll be on my way, too.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.360
Oh, hang on a second.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:21.140
You forgot this. A minced 
meat cutlet sandwich.

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:24.010
Oh! I forgot all about it!

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:25.360
And one more thing.

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:27.320
What's that?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.960
Corn potage.

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:31.450
Sorry it's just leftovers, 
but take it home and eat it.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:36.080
Thank you so much!

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:40.720
Come to think of it, I haven't 
seen Sarah-san lately.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:42.000
Has she been busy?

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.960
Yes, though I don't know all the details...

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:50.290
Apparently, some texts containing 
hints about a treasure were released,

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:52.840
and she's been glued to her desk ever since.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:56.440
She hasn't eaten much, either. It worries me.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.110
I'm back!

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:19.690
Sarah-san?

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:35.960
Uh... I don't understand a word of this.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:01.150
<i>Sarah-san has done so much for me.</i>

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:04.340
<i>Is there nothing I can do for her?</i>

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.360
<i>Like massage her shoulders,</i>

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:10.840
<i>or make her some tea...</i>

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:13.880
<i>I always do those things, though.</i>

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:15.750
<i>Oh!</i>

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.570
<i>I could stick close by and cheer for her!</i>

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:23.850
<i>Wait, that would just 
bother her, wouldn't it?</i>

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:28.850
<i>I know!</i>

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:44.250
It's morning... Huh?

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:51.270
Oh... I guess I fell asleep before 
Aletta came home last night.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.570
I'm hungry.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:58.360
I haven't eaten anything

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:02.670
since that stale rye bread and dry 
cheese I had for lunch yesterday.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:07.420
What is that sweet smell?

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:15.280
Good morning, Sarah-san!

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.010
Morning, Aletta.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.050
Breakfast will be ready soon.

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:21.020
Wait just a bit longer, okay?

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:22.210
Thanks.

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.790
What is this soup, by the way?

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:28.630
Oh, the master sent some 
home with me last night.

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:31.420
Yeah? Well, that's something 
to look forward to.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.030
How's your work going?

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:36.500
Nowhere.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:40.050
But a job this difficult is 
all the more worth doing.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:43.050
Sarah-san, do you know what the treasure is?

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:45.910
I won't until I open it.

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.900
What would you like it to be?

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:48.810
Huh?

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:51.640
I guess I'd like, um...

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.440
Maybe 100 gold coins!

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:59.770
Wait, no! I think I'd say 
my current lifestyle!

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:04.710
I don't think there's anything 
I really want that much, though.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:08.620
So even if I end up making an 
enormous fortune off of this job,

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:12.210
I should continue paying you 
the same amount I am now?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.160
Actually, uh...

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:16.560
I'm just kidding.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:21.470
<i>Breakfast Again</i>

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:27.470
Thank you, god of demons, 
for this, my daily bread.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:28.680
I shall now partake.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.880
Yes, let's eat.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:37.080
<i>Just toasting it over a flame 
really makes a huge difference.</i>

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:39.990
<i>When it's just me, I end up eating it as is.</i>

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.710
<i>The cheese is much better this way, too!</i>

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.460
<i>And now...</i>

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:59.200
<i>It seems like it'll be a bit sweet.</i>

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.440
<i>I don't like the kind of 
sweets we had back home,</i>

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:04.910
<i>the ones so sweet they made 
my head and teeth hurt.</i>

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:12.130
<i>But this level of sweetness 
tastes good to me!</i>

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.850
<i>It's like the fruit of the other world,
but different from our fruit.</i>

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:17.940
<i>The sweetness of milk and sweet vegetables.</i>

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:19.980
<i>The more I taste it,</i>

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:22.510
<i>the more I notice the saltiness 
behind the sweetness,</i>

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:26.130
<i>as well as the mellowness of milk 
and the savoriness of oranie.</i>

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:29.470
<i>Complex seasonings that restaurant 
uses in soups other than miso soup</i>

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:32.520
<i>are dissolved throughout it.</i>

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:38.920
<i>Dipping the bread in the 
soup makes it softer.</i>

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.170
<i>The soup bursts out with every bite,</i>

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:44.690
<i>making this everyday rye 
bread a luxurious feast!</i>

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.080
<i>Yes, it's delicious!</i>

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:06.570
<i>I think this just might be...</i>

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:09.080
<i>Aletta's favorite?</i>

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.160
Here. All yours.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.050
Huh? Are you sure?

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:18.040
Yes.

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.890
Thank you so much!

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:25.090
By the way, did you buy 
the thing I asked for?

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:26.080
Of course!

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.910
I'll serve your minced meat 
cutlet sandwich for lunch!

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:30.890
Thanks.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.910
I think I'd like to eat it now, though.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:33.680
Huh?

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.430
But if you eat that much, 
won't your stomach...

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:45.130
Got it! Give me just a moment!

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:50.200
Here you go! Your minced 
meat cutlet sandwich!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:53.700
Yeah, this is it! 
Minced meat cutlet is the best!

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:58.710
You really love minced 
meat cutlets, don't you?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:42.440
<i>Beefsteak</i>

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Cream Puffs</i>
